			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1415527">
									

<p>That's actually just about what I had in my head! The person doing it was a definite subscriber to the theory of &quot;Knowledge is power; guard it well&quot;, and probably would have only even written the simple premise to spread it more easily, a necessary evil from his/her standpoint. Of course, being a complete narcissist, the simple premise ended up becoming a rant spanning <em>four hardbound volumes</em>. Somewhere along the line, the insanity of it all twisted up the very rules of the universe and the books became the embodiement of the philosophy itself, burning all other sources of knowledge and leaving only itself intact.</p>
<p>&#8230;. Of course there's literally no possible way for the Foundation to acquire this information beyond what may have been written in the books, so it won't turn up in any official statements, and thus shouldn't bind anyone else's head-canon ;)</p>

